Chapter: BvtHitSound
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 Damian, 2026-10-10: the smith hammer "makes sword sounds". A human's hit sound follows the weapon's class (UOX3
 PlayHitSoundEffect): mace fighting 0x232, archery 0x234, a one-handed blade 0x23B, a two-handed one 0x237, no weapon 0x135.
  bvt-hit-sound : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-hit-sound (unused) = when cg-new 0
    is Err (e) -> bvt-check ("hit sound fixture: " & e) False
    is Ok (owner) -> let c = owner.combat
      in let hammer = cb-hit-sound c 400 1 (wpn-stats #13E3)
      in let mace = cb-hit-sound c 400 1 (wpn-stats #0F5C)
      in let sword = cb-hit-sound c 400 1 (wpn-stats #0F61)
      in let fist = cb-hit-sound c 400 0 0 in act
      print-line-uni ("HITSOUND hammer=" & show hammer & " mace=" & show mace & " sword=" & show sword & " fist=" & show fist)
      a <- bvt-check "the smith hammer and the mace hit with the mace sound, the longsword with the sword sound, a fist with the punch" (wpn-stats #13E3 /= 0 & hammer == #0232 & mace == #0232 & sword == #023B & fist == #0135)
      a
    end
